==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*swait-}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*swoyd-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*sweyd-}}. Cognate with Old Saxon {{term|swêt|lang=osx}}, Old High German {{term|sweiz|lang=goh}}, Old Norse {{term|sveiti||sweat, blood|lang=non}}. The Indo-European root also gave Latin {{term|sudor|lang=la}}, Sanskrit {{term|स्वेद|tr=sveda|lang=sa}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/swaːt/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|m|head=swāt}}

# [[blood]]

